        "short_description": "Generic 30-team professional baseball league: two leagues of three five-team divisions, a 162-game regular season, six postseason places per league (three division winners and three wild cards), best-of-3/5/7/7 bracket. Rename the competition and the placeholder teams during onboarding."
      },
      "lore": [
        {
          "title": "Structure",
          "content": "Two leagues (League A, League B), each with East, Central and West divisions of five teams. Each season the league is the conference on the team's COMPETES_IN edge (\"League A\") and the division is its group (\"East\"); the standing league and division are tags on the team (league-a, league-a-east). Postseason: wildcard (best of three), divisional (best of five), league_championship (best of seven), final (best of seven). Vocabulary: rule/sport_baseball. Teams are placeholders named Team 1 to Team 30; rename them (names drive slugs, so rename before adding anything that points at them) and set city, short_name and abbreviation. Install at most one league shape with Team N placeholders per world, or rename before installing a second.",
          "display_index": 0
        }
      ]
    },
